      },
      "source": [
        "### c. Vocabulary Handling & Unknown Words\n",
        "\n",
        "In this section, we build the vocabulary from the training set and identify all unique POS tags. This is crucial for constructing the HMM matrices. We'll also prepare a strategy for handling unknown words that appear in the test set but not in the training set."
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "code",
      "metadata": {
        "colab": {
          "base_uri": "https://localhost:8080/"
        },
        "id": "88f6ba1f",
        "outputId": "79981ca8-916a-4c8d-d7ae-0bf60814ae6e"
      },
      "source": [
        "# Create vocabulary from training data\n",
        "# Use a set for efficient lookup\n",
        "vocabulary = set(train_words)\n",
        "\n",
        "# Get all unique POS tags from the training data\n",
        "# This will represent the hidden states in our HMM\n",
        "all_pos_tags = list(set(train_tags))\n",
        "all_pos_tags.sort() # Sort for consistent ordering\n",
        "\n",
        "print(f\"Size of vocabulary (unique words from training data): {len(vocabulary)}\")\n",
        "print(f\"Number of unique POS tags: {len(all_pos_tags)}\")\n",
        "print(\"\\nSample of unique POS tags:\")\n",
        "print(all_pos_tags[:10]) # Print first 10 tags for brevity"
      ],
      "execution_count": 31,
      "outputs": [
        {
          "output_type": "stream",
          "name": "stdout",
          "text": [
            "Size of vocabulary (unique words from training data): 13112\n",
            "Number of unique POS tags: 12\n",
            "\n",
            "Sample of unique POS tags:\n",
            "['.', 'ADJ', 'ADP', 'ADV', 'CONJ', 'DET', 'NOUN', 'NUM', 'PRON', 'PRT']\n"
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "metadata": {
        "id": "d216a87b"
      },
      "source": [
        "To handle unknown words (Out-Of-Vocabulary or OOV words) in the test set, we will replace them with a special token, typically `\"_UNKNOWN_\"`. This allows the HMM to assign probabilities to these words during inference."
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "code",
      "metadata": {
        "colab": {
          "base_uri": "https://localhost:8080/"
        },
        "id": "3ab20c91",
        "outputId": "57c1c136-5058-4cd3-8419-b6cfc147509f"
      },
      "source": [
        "# Define a special token for unknown words\n",
        "UNKNOWN_TOKEN = '_UNKNOWN_'\n",
        "\n",
        "# Function to replace OOV words in sentences\n",
        "def handle_oov_words(sentences, vocab):\n",
        "    processed_sentences = []\n",
        "    for sent in sentences:\n",
        "        processed_sent = []\n",
        "        for word, tag in sent:\n",
        "            # Convert word to lowercase for consistency\n",
        "            processed_word = word.lower()\n",
        "            if processed_word not in vocab:\n",
        "                processed_sent.append((UNKNOWN_TOKEN, tag))\n",
        "            else:\n",
        "                processed_sent.append((processed_word, tag))\n",
        "        processed_sentences.append(processed_sent)\n",
        "    return processed_sentences\n",
        "\n",
        "# Apply OOV handling to the test sentences\n",
        "test_sentences_processed = handle_oov_words(test_sentences_raw, vocabulary)\n",
        "\n",
        "# Add UNKNOWN_TOKEN to the vocabulary for proper emission probability calculation\n",
        "vocabulary.add(UNKNOWN_TOKEN)\n",
        "\n",
        "print(f\"Test sentences after OOV handling (first sentence):\")\n",
        "print(test_sentences_processed[0])\n",
        "print(f\"\\nNew vocabulary size after adding UNKNOWN_TOKEN: {len(vocabulary)}\")\n",
        "\n",
        "# Check for OOV words in the first few test sentences\n",
        "oov_count = 0\n",
        "for i, (word, tag) in enumerate(test_sentences_processed[0]):\n",
        "    if word == UNKNOWN_TOKEN:\n",
        "        oov_count += 1\n",
        "        print(f\"  OOV word found: {test_sentences_raw[0][i][0]} replaced by {UNKNOWN_TOKEN}\")\n",
        "\n",
        "if oov_count == 0:\n",
        "    print(\"No OOV words found in the first test sentence.\")"
      ],
      "execution_count": 32,
      "outputs": [
        {
          "output_type": "stream",
          "name": "stdout",
          "text": [
            "Test sentences after OOV handling (first sentence):\n",
            "[('_UNKNOWN_', 'NUM')]\n",
            "\n",
            "New vocabulary size after adding UNKNOWN_TOKEN: 13113\n",
            "  OOV word found: Thirty-three replaced by _UNKNOWN_\n"
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "metadata": {
        "id": "d28dc937"
      },
      "source": [
        "### d. Sentence Padding\n",
        "\n",
        "To handle the start and end of sentences in our HMM, we will pad each sentence with special tokens: `('<s>', '<s>')` for the beginning and `('</s>', '</s>')` for the end. This allows for proper calculation of initial and final state transition probabilities."
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "code",
      "metadata": {
        "colab": {
          "base_uri": "https://localhost:8080/"
        },
        "id": "60cd0f2f",
        "outputId": "3d065536-b5a9-4cf5-eff6-4e37b5ed3c51"
      },
      "source": [
        "# Define start and end tokens for sentence padding\n",
        "START_TOKEN = '<s>'\n",
        "END_TOKEN = '</s>'\n",
        "\n",
        "# Function to pad sentences with start and end tokens\n",
        "def pad_sentences(sentences):\n",
        "    padded_sentences = []\n",
        "    for sent in sentences:\n",
        "        padded_sentences.append([(START_TOKEN, START_TOKEN)] + sent + [(END_TOKEN, END_TOKEN)])\n",
        "    return padded_sentences\n",
        "\n",
        "# Apply padding to training and processed test sentences\n",
        "train_sentences_padded = pad_sentences(train_sentences)\n",
        "test_sentences_processed_padded = pad_sentences(test_sentences_processed)\n",
        "\n",
        "print(f\"Original first training sentence: {train_sentences[0]}\\n\")\n",
        "print(f\"Padded first training sentence: {train_sentences_padded[0]}\\n\")\n",
        "\n",
        "print(f\"Original first test sentence: {test_sentences_raw[0]}\\n\")\n",
        "print(f\"Padded first test sentence (after OOV handling): {test_sentences_processed_padded[0]}\\n\")"
      ],
      "execution_count": 33,
      "outputs": [
        {
          "output_type": "stream",
          "name": "stdout",
          "text": [
