    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "metadata": {
        "id": "c1906ab7"
      },
      "source": [
        "## Part 2: Model Architecture & Parameter Estimation\n",
        "\n",
        "This section focuses on building a fundamental Bigram Hidden Markov Model from scratch. We will estimate the Transition Probability Matrix (A) and Emission Probability Matrix (B) using Maximum Likelihood Estimation (MLE) from the training data."
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "metadata": {
        "id": "fbad868e"
      },
      "source": [
        "### Estimate the Transition Probability Matrix (A)\n",
        "\n",
        "The Transition Probability Matrix $A_{ij}$ represents the probability of transitioning from state (POS tag) $i$ to state (POS tag) $j$. We estimate this using Maximum Likelihood Estimation (MLE) based on the observed tag sequences in the training data:\n",
        "\n",
        "$A_{ij} = P(tag_j | tag_i) = \\frac{Count(tag_i, tag_j)}{Count(tag_i)}$\n",
        "\n",
        "We include the start (`<s>`) and end (`</s>`) tokens in our tag set to handle sentence boundaries."
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "code",
      "metadata": {
        "colab": {
          "base_uri": "https://localhost:8080/",
          "height": 996
        },
        "id": "9b043eca",
        "outputId": "dccc68b3-332a-4c0f-cffe-72763e514224"
      },
      "source": [
        "# Initialize counts for transitions\n",
        "tag_tag_counts = defaultdict(lambda: defaultdict(int))\n",
        "tag_counts = defaultdict(int)\n",
        "\n",
        "# Populate tag_tag_counts and tag_counts from the training data\n",
        "for sent in train_sentences_padded:\n",
        "    for i in range(len(sent) - 1):\n",
        "        current_tag = sent[i][1] # Current POS tag\n",
        "        next_tag = sent[i+1][1]  # Next POS tag\n",
        "\n",
        "        tag_tag_counts[current_tag][next_tag] += 1\n",
        "        tag_counts[current_tag] += 1\n",
        "\n",
        "# Calculate Transition Probability Matrix (A)\n",
        "# A[current_tag][next_tag] = P(next_tag | current_tag)\n",
        "transition_probabilities = defaultdict(lambda: defaultdict(float))\n",
        "\n",
        "for current_tag, next_tags in tag_tag_counts.items():\n",
        "    total_current_tag_count = tag_counts[current_tag]\n",
        "    for next_tag, count in next_tags.items():\n",
        "        transition_probabilities[current_tag][next_tag] = count / total_current_tag_count\n",
        "\n",
        "print(\"Sample Transition Probabilities:\")\n",
        "print(f\"P(NOUN | DET): {transition_probabilities['DET']['NOUN']:.4f}\")\n",
        "print(f\"P(VERB | NOUN): {transition_probabilities['NOUN']['VERB']:.4f}\")\n",
