      "source": [
        "### Estimate the Emission Probability Matrix (B)\n",
        "\n",
        "The Emission Probability Matrix $B_{jk}$ represents the probability of observing a word $k$ given a state (POS tag) $j$. Similar to the transition matrix, we estimate this using Maximum Likelihood Estimation (MLE) from the training data:\n",
        "\n",
        "$B_{jk} = P(word_k | tag_j) = \\frac{Count(tag_j, word_k)}{Count(tag_j)}$\n",
        "\n",
        "We will also handle the `_UNKNOWN_` token here, assigning a small probability to it for all tags to avoid zero probabilities for unseen words in the test set."
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "code",
      "metadata": {
        "colab": {
          "base_uri": "https://localhost:8080/"
        },
        "id": "caa8ddf9",
        "outputId": "d204c2da-da75-4519-b92c-a42962ce38f0"
      },
      "source": [
        "# Initialize counts for emissions\n",
        "tag_word_counts = defaultdict(lambda: defaultdict(int))\n",
        "tag_frequencies_for_emission = defaultdict(int) # New dictionary to correctly count tag occurrences for emission\n",
        "\n",
        "# Populate tag_word_counts and tag_frequencies_for_emission\n",
        "for sent in train_sentences_padded:\n",
        "    for word, tag in sent:\n",
        "        # Only process actual content words/tags for emission probabilities.\n",
        "        # Special START_TOKEN and END_TOKEN do not emit words, so they are excluded.\n",
        "        if tag not in [START_TOKEN, END_TOKEN]:\n",
        "            word_lower = word.lower()\n",
        "            tag_word_counts[tag][word_lower] += 1\n",
        "            tag_frequencies_for_emission[tag] += 1 # Count every occurrence of the tag\n",
        "\n",
        "# Calculate Emission Probability Matrix (B)\n",
        "# B[tag][word] = P(word | tag)\n",
        "emission_probabilities = defaultdict(lambda: defaultdict(float))\n",
        "\n",
        "ALPHA = 1e-6 # A small constant for smoothing unknown words\n",
        "\n",
        "for tag, words in tag_word_counts.items():\n",
        "    total_tag_count = tag_frequencies_for_emission[tag] # Use the new, correct tag count\n",
        "\n",
        "    # This check ensures we don't divide by zero if, somehow, a tag with word counts has zero total frequency\n",
        "    if total_tag_count == 0:\n",
        "        continue\n",
        "\n",
        "    # Calculate probabilities for known words\n",
        "    for word, count in words.items():\n",
        "        emission_probabilities[tag][word] = count / total_tag_count\n",
        "\n",
        "    # Handle UNKNOWN_TOKEN: assign a small, non-zero probability to it for every tag.\n",
        "    # This loop iterates over keys from tag_word_counts, which already excludes START/END_TOKEN.\n",
        "    emission_probabilities[tag][UNKNOWN_TOKEN] = ALPHA # Assign a small probability to the OOV token\n",
        "\n",
        "print(\"Sample Emission Probabilities:\")\n",
        "print(f\"P('the' | DET): {emission_probabilities['DET']['the']:.4f}\")\n",
        "print(f\"P('run' | VERB): {emission_probabilities['VERB']['run']:.4f}\")\n",
        "print(f\"P('car' | NOUN): {emission_probabilities['NOUN']['car']:.4f}\")\n",
        "print(f\"P('_UNKNOWN_' | NOUN): {emission_probabilities['NOUN'][UNKNOWN_TOKEN]:.6f}\")\n",
        "\n",
        "# Convert to DataFrame for better visualization (optional)\n",
        "# For emission matrix, it's very sparse due to large vocabulary, so showing a small sample is better\n",
        "\n",
        "# Create a small sample DataFrame for common tags and words\n",
        "sample_tags = ['DET', 'NOUN', 'VERB', 'ADJ', 'ADP']\n",
        "sample_words = ['the', 'a', 'man', 'car', 'run', 'walk', 'good', 'bad', 'in', 'on', UNKNOWN_TOKEN]\n",
        "\n",
        "emission_data = {word: [emission_probabilities[tag][word] for tag in sample_tags] for word in sample_words}\n",
        "emission_df = pd.DataFrame(emission_data, index=sample_tags).fillna(0)\n",
        "\n",
        "print(\"\\nEmission Probability Matrix (Sample):\\n\")\n",
        "print(emission_df)\n"
      ],
      "execution_count": 36,
