      "source": [
        "### Implement the Viterbi Algorithm\n",
        "\n",
        "The Viterbi algorithm is a dynamic programming algorithm for finding the most likely sequence of hidden states (Viterbi path) that results in a sequence of observed events, especially in the context of Hidden Markov Models (HMMs).\n",
        "\n",
        "Here's a high-level overview of the steps:\n",
        "1.  **Initialization**: For the first word, calculate the probability of each POS tag being the starting tag and emitting the first word.\n",
        "2.  **Recursion**: For each subsequent word, and for each possible current POS tag, calculate the maximum probability of reaching this tag, given all previous paths and the probability of emitting the current word.\n",
        "3.  **Termination**: Find the most probable sequence ending with the end-of-sentence token.\n",
        "4.  **Path Backtracking**: Reconstruct the sequence of POS tags by backtracking through the stored paths."
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "code",
      "metadata": {
        "id": "f9011891"
      },
      "source": [
        "def viterbi(words, all_pos_tags, transition_probabilities, emission_probabilities, vocabulary, START_TOKEN, END_TOKEN, UNKNOWN_TOKEN, ALPHA):\n",
        "    \"\"\"\n",
        "    Implements the Viterbi algorithm to find the most likely sequence of POS tags for a given sequence of words.\n",
        "\n",
        "    Args:\n",
        "        words (list): A list of words (observations) in a sentence.\n",
        "        all_pos_tags (list): A list of all possible POS tags (states), excluding START/END tokens.\n",
        "        transition_probabilities (defaultdict): P(tag_j | tag_i).\n",
        "        emission_probabilities (defaultdict): P(word_k | tag_j).\n",
        "        vocabulary (set): Set of all known words, including UNKNOWN_TOKEN.\n",
        "        START_TOKEN (str): Special token for the start of a sentence.\n",
        "        END_TOKEN (str): Special token for the end of a sentence.\n",
        "        UNKNOWN_TOKEN (str): Special token for out-of-vocabulary words.\n",
        "        ALPHA (float): Small constant for handling unknown word emissions.\n",
        "\n",
        "    Returns:\n",
        "        tuple: A tuple containing the most likely sequence of POS tags and its probability.\n",
        "    \"\"\"\n",
        "\n",
        "    # Number of words in the sentence and number of possible POS tags\n",
        "    num_words = len(words)\n",
        "    # Filter out START_TOKEN and END_TOKEN from all_pos_tags for Viterbi processing,\n",
        "    # as these are boundary tags and not actual POS tags for words.\n",
        "    viterbi_tags = [tag for tag in all_pos_tags if tag not in [START_TOKEN, END_TOKEN]]\n",
        "    num_tags = len(viterbi_tags)\n",
        "\n",
        "    # Create a mapping from tag string to its index for efficient NumPy array access\n",
        "    tag_to_idx = {tag: i for i, tag in enumerate(viterbi_tags)}\n",
        "    idx_to_tag = {i: tag for i, tag in enumerate(viterbi_tags)}\n",
        "\n",
        "    # Initialize Viterbi table and backpointer table\n",
        "    # viterbi_table[t][tag_idx] stores the maximum probability of a tag sequence ending with tag_idx at time t\n",
        "    # backpointer[t][tag_idx] stores the index of the previous tag that led to the maximum probability\n",
        "    viterbi_table = np.zeros((num_words, num_tags))\n",
        "    backpointer = np.zeros((num_words, num_tags), dtype=int)\n",
        "\n",
        "    # --- Initialization Step (t = 0) ---\n",
        "    # For the first word, calculate the probability of each POS tag being the first tag\n",
        "    # P(tag_i | START_TOKEN) * P(word_0 | tag_i)\n",
        "    first_word = words[0].lower()\n",
        "\n",
        "    for i, current_tag in enumerate(viterbi_tags):\n",
        "        # Probability of transitioning from START_TOKEN to current_tag\n",
        "        prob_start_to_tag = transition_probabilities[START_TOKEN].get(current_tag, ALPHA)\n",
        "\n",
        "        # Emission probability of the first word given the current_tag\n",
        "        # If the word is OOV and becomes UNKNOWN_TOKEN, its probability is ALPHA (set during emission matrix calc).\n",
        "        # If the word is a known word not seen with this tag, use ALPHA for smoothing.\n",
        "        prob_word_given_tag = emission_probabilities[current_tag].get(first_word, emission_probabilities[current_tag].get(UNKNOWN_TOKEN, ALPHA))\n",
        "\n",
        "        viterbi_table[0, i] = prob_start_to_tag * prob_word_given_tag\n",
        "        # No backpointer for t=0\n",
        "\n",
        "    # --- Recursion Step (t = 1 to num_words - 1) ---\n",
        "    # For each subsequent word, calculate the maximum probability for each possible current tag\n",
        "    for t in range(1, num_words):\n",
        "        current_word = words[t].lower()\n",
        "\n",
        "        for j, current_tag in enumerate(viterbi_tags):\n",
        "            max_prob = 0\n",
        "            best_prev_tag_idx = 0\n",
        "\n",
        "            # Emission probability of the current word given the current_tag\n",
        "            prob_word_given_tag = emission_probabilities[current_tag].get(current_word, emission_probabilities[current_tag].get(UNKNOWN_TOKEN, ALPHA))\n",
        "\n",
        "            for i, prev_tag in enumerate(viterbi_tags):\n",
        "                # Probability of path to previous tag * transition from prev_tag to current_tag * emission of current_word\n",
        "                prob = viterbi_table[t-1, i] * transition_probabilities[prev_tag].get(current_tag, ALPHA) * prob_word_given_tag\n",
        "\n",
        "                if prob > max_prob:\n",
        "                    max_prob = prob\n",
        "                    best_prev_tag_idx = i\n",
        "\n",
        "            viterbi_table[t, j] = max_prob\n",
        "            backpointer[t, j] = best_prev_tag_idx\n",
        "\n",
        "    # --- Termination Step ---\n",
        "    # Find the maximum probability of a path ending with a transition to END_TOKEN\n",
        "    max_final_prob = 0\n",
        "    last_tag_of_best_path_idx = 0\n",
        "\n",
        "    for i, last_possible_tag in enumerate(viterbi_tags):\n",
        "        # P(path_to_last_tag) * P(END_TOKEN | last_tag)\n",
        "        prob = viterbi_table[num_words-1, i] * transition_probabilities[last_possible_tag].get(END_TOKEN, ALPHA)\n",
        "        if prob > max_final_prob:\n",
        "            max_final_prob = prob\n",
        "            last_tag_of_best_path_idx = i\n",
        "\n",
        "    # --- Path Backtracking ---\n",
        "    # Reconstruct the best tag sequence by backtracking from the last tag\n",
        "    best_path_tags = [idx_to_tag[last_tag_of_best_path_idx]]\n",
        "    for t in range(num_words - 1, 0, -1):\n",
        "        last_tag_of_best_path_idx = backpointer[t, last_tag_of_best_path_idx]\n",
        "        best_path_tags.insert(0, idx_to_tag[last_tag_of_best_path_idx]) # Insert at the beginning\n",
        "\n",
        "    return best_path_tags, max_final_prob"
      ],
      "execution_count": 37,
      "outputs": []
    },
